{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPnCp9cakVcvjb5qYMF2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01898uM6uHhi2yNdLZLHY4S4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"The executor is not an effect: dry-run runs it as local jobs run today.\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"The executor is not an effect: it never calls GitHub to change anything, and dry-run runs it as local jobs run today. The k8s executor mints and revokes read tokens, which are credentials, not effects.\",1)\nlines=s.split('\\n')\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('**Controller.** `Prepare` builds the local workspace.')][0]\nnew='''**Serve wiring ([#318](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/318)).** `executor:` in `.ard/config.yaml` picks the executor at startup and it is fixed for the life of the process: a later config whose `executor` differs is a config error (serve pauses, the status issue says `restart ard serve`). Cluster settings are `ard serve` flags with `ARD_K8S_*` env fallbacks, set by the chart: `--k8s-namespace`, `--k8s-instance`, `--k8s-agent-image`, `--k8s-pod-image` (both images pinned by `@sha256:` digest), `--k8s-git-base` (default `https://github.com`), `--k8s-resources` (`cpu=`, `memory=`, `memory-limit=`, `ephemeral-storage=` for the agent container), `--k8s-pre-budget` (5m) and `--k8s-result-grace` (2m). With `executor: k8s`, startup fails (exit 1) if the credential is a personal access token (also under `--dry-run`), a required flag is missing, or the config sets `roles_repo` (not supported with k8s yet). If no config has loaded and the cluster flags are set, the mode is unknown and no job loops are built until restart (`serve.executor_unresolved`). At startup the `pool-adopt` hook calls the executor's `Sweep`, which deletes this repo's job pods and Secrets that no running job record owns; pods with a record go through the Reaper's normal `Orphaned` path. The Reaper maps the executor's end reasons to causes: `evicted` (pod evicted, deleted or never scheduled; transient, one automatic retry), `clone_failed` (transient), and `no_process` for a failed prep step, bad result or missing result. Inputs over the manifest cap close out as `inputs_too_large` and are not retried. Live read tokens are added to the redaction set. `ard config check` prints a note that cluster settings come from `ard serve` flags.'''\nlines.insert(i,new)\nlines.insert(i+1,'')\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(lines))\np='docs/layout.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"registerLoops takes one line per loop\"\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"; picks the local or Kubernetes executor from `executor:` and sweeps orphan pods at startup\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; go test ./... 2>&1 | grep -v \"^ok\\|no test files\\|downloading\" | head -30","timeout":580000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7547,"cache_read_input_tokens":106698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7547},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbda8032-e3d0-4031-9912-0f0db5a7fd12","uuid":"f5a9c3d3-2ecc-4443-9bec-d72e20327a97","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:10:20.574Z","request_id":"req_011ChPnCozBhg5w2pJ2KxVAY"}
